description:
Gated final-SHA live stress of mod delivery in real Claude TUI sessions with evidence, read-only fallback to unit stress.
Spec docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-09-claude-mod-inbound-delivery/2026-10-09-claude-mod-inbound-delivery-design.md D10 (live). Final-SHA evidence. tests/native/claude_mod/stress.py: drive real Claude Code TUI sessions in a private tmux server (tmux -L <unique>) with an isolated signed-in CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, the installed mod (CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS) and an isolated herdr-threads daemon/state dir plus HERDR_PANE_ID from an isolated Herdr test session (scripts/lib/isolated-herdr.sh) or a fake pane id if the daemon permits; N iterations (default 20 each) of: send during busy turn (expect context delivery + ack), send while idle (submit + ack), lazy send (append, no turn), queued user prompt at turn end, Stop-hook continuation, Esc interrupt with pending message (expect hold, no takeover), permission dialog open, /clear and /resume (rebind, no duplicate), reload, kill watch child (fallback to native wake path, then reconnect re-stream without duplicates). Assert from daemon receipts + mod debug ledger: no duplicate deliveries/acks, no submit while busy, every message settled or still pending (never lost). Write evidence to docs/evidence/claude-mod-delivery/. Uses disable autoupdater env. Never touches the shared Herdr server or real ~/.claude. Profile: a signed-in isolated profile exists at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-alepar-AleCode-herdr-threads/6ac583b8-5b3a-4ce5-9809-728b586f23fc/scratchpad/modspike/profile (copy it to a temp dir per run; do not modify the original). Read-only fallback when no signed-in profile is usable: run only the mod unit-level randomized stress (claude plugin test) and record the live gap in the evidence file. Stops every process it starts.
